Dome Dialog
===========
Native FLTK replacement for the Zenity command subset used by Winetricks.
Built with CMake Release against /opt/fltk-vr/toolkit and the shared DomeD
appearance headers in ../flterm-xr/xr. The installed command is /usr/bin/zenity;
the package provides zenity=4.2.2 to preserve Winetricks dependencies.

Supported modes: info, warning, error, question, entry/password, list with
radiolist/checklist and hidden/printed columns, forms with entries/combos,
progress from standard input, file selection, and text display. Output uses
the requested separators. Timeout exits 5; unsupported options exit 2.
This is a tested subset, not a promise of the entire Zenity command API.

Build and stage as the regular user:
  cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build
  DESTDIR="$PWD/stage" cmake --install build
Only installation into system paths needs sudo. No GTK or Qt is linked.
The GPL-3.0-or-later license applies to main.cpp; shared appearance headers
retain their own MIT license. Build the RPM with python3 tools/package.py build. Seven isolated UI checks
run with python3 tools/test-dialogs.py build/dome-dialog.
